id: pm-web-h4vh
title: Investigate the remaining mixed-writer latency tail at 1000 subscribers
description: "Package-owned follow-up to PR #226 and companion pm-cli-website-ghe1. Implement shared UTF-8 project frames, bounded burst coalescing, isolated per-viewer backpressure and resumable Last-Event-ID replay without weakening private-project authorization. Attribute the existing write/detection/route/response path and compare 100/1000/3000 real authenticated SSE viewers with mixed HTTP and separate pinned CLI writers using interleaved A/B/A/B runs, CPU microseconds per delivered frame, encoded bytes, event-loop delay and host load. Preserve full npm/Bun release thresholds, record behavioral revert proof and public-safe raw evidence, and leave the PR unmerged. Hosted services and the companion tracker are outside this package task."
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: capacity,performance,realtime
created_at: "2026-10-15T09:09:03.386Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T01:07:57.220Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[71]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T08:11:29.603Z",codex-agent,"Additional real-PostgreSQL acceptance evidence from the route/bootstrap coverage candidate: the second final-floor npm run passes all 634 coverage tests and all four dimensions, then fails only test/capacity.acceptance.ts line 16: every delivery must meet the unchanged 2000 ms SLO. Earlier assertions pass for five committed writes, zero failed writes/lost/disconnected subscribers/duplicates, and five delivery samples. This is latency failure evidence, not mutation-loss evidence. The first final-floor npm and Bun gates pass, and both Node 22/26 CI matrix jobs pass their npm and Bun release gates on source/test commit e053bb1. Reproduction: npm run release:check with isolated Git identity and explicit fleet discovery; the second Bun repetition is still running. No SLO, capacity assertion or production behavior was changed."
  "2026-10-16T09:06:30.996Z",codex-agent,"Measuring unchanged origin/main first: three isolated 100-subscriber runs, 10 mixed writer lanes and 50 updates. Production watcher defaults and disposable test Postgres only. Then attribute each delivery stage, implement a measured repair if package-owned, prove behavioural revert, and repeat the ladder. No hosted resources or other agents are used."
  "2026-10-16T09:09:17.778Z",codex-agent,"Unchanged baseline at 3336ef6: three 100-subscriber runs all committed 50/50 writes with loss=0, duplicates=0. To-all p50/p95/p99/max ms: 145.3/583.0/1181.3/1181.3; 220.4/594.0/898.9/898.9; 149.7/462.9/913.2/913.2. Loop p99 22.0/25.1/24.2 ms; CPU p95 35.2/26.5/39.8 percent of one core; RSS 194.8/195.3/195.1 MiB. Initial uptime loads: 3.43,4.78,6.86; 4.73,4.94,6.83; 9.18,5.90,7.08. Historical 2163.5 ms breach did not reproduce. CLI tail exceeds HTTP; fan-out already shares serialization with no per-client awaits/auth reads. Next: opt-in test-only stage tracing including SDK index-lock waits and history append visibility, without changing production defaults."
  "2026-10-16T09:19:22.579Z",codex-agent,"Three valid traced 100-subscriber runs: p50/p95/p99/max ms 198.5/485.5/633.9/633.9; 308.2/1492.4/2965.8/2965.8; 245.0/956.1/1239.2/1239.2. All 50/50 writes committed; zero loss/duplicates. Breach reproduced in trace run 2: CLI timestamp-to-history-append p99 2247.5 ms, including index-file-lock acquisition lower bound p99 2071.0 ms; detecting read/classification p99 1106.7 ms; polling wait p99 232.4 ms. Shared serialization p99 HTTP/CLI 1.45/9.50 ms; client write p99 0.048/0.025 ms. The pinned SDK serializes history-index readers and appenders on an exclusive index-file lock before authoritative history append. No safe pm-web hot-path repair is justified by this evidence; preserve replay/dedupe/authorization unchanged, draft upstream issue here without filing it. Stop expansion at 100 after SLO breach; 250/500/1000 remain unmeasured. Three earlier full traces and two small diagnostic runs were inconclusive while validating probes and are excluded. Raw reports remain external; public-safe summary and methods will be committed."
  "2026-10-16T09:22:04.470Z",codex-agent,"DRAFT UPSTREAM ISSUE (not filed). Title: Mixed history-index readers and writers can delay authoritative append beyond a 2-second delivery budget. Package: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.15. Reproduce with the public pm-web capacity harness, disposable test Postgres, 100 authenticated SSE readers, five HTTP SDK writer lanes and five separate pinned CLI writer lanes, five independent item updates each; retain ordinary 250 ms mutation polling and 60-second inclusive replay. docs/capacity/2026-10-16-local.md records three untraced p99 values 1181.3/898.9/913.2 ms and three traced values 633.9/2965.8/1239.2 ms. In the breached run, all 50 updates and 5000 receipts arrived exactly once. CLI timestamp-to-authoritative-append p99/max 2247.5 ms independently exceeds the total 2000 ms SLO; index-file-lock wait lower bound p99/max is 2071.0 ms. Detecting SDK read/classification p99 1106.7 ms, polling wait p99 232.4 ms; per-client write p99 under 0.05 ms. Implementation inspection: queryHistoryEventIndex and appendHistoryEntryWithEventIndex both acquire withHistoryEventIndexLock; append acquires before authoritative history write and queries validate stream sizes under that exclusive lock. Expected: committed-fact readers should not introduce unbounded writer latency or visibility loss. Investigate a validated nonblocking/read snapshot strategy or fair lock acquisition while preserving authoritative fallback and late-fact visibility; do not remove validation or timestamp overlap blindly. Clock starts before persistence by harness contract, not at fsync or response. Shared-host scheduling and probe perturbation remain confounders; reader-versus-writer contention contribution and the original busy-host breach are not separately proven. No upstream mutation or filing performed."
  "2026-10-16T09:22:20.191Z",codex-agent,"Linked tests pass: stage-accounting regressions 2/2 and real-process capacity acceptance 2/2 (ordinary 20-subscriber smoke plus traced HTTP/CLI probe coverage). Test-result tracking is disabled by project policy, so the linked runner reports execution receipts without persisting test-run metadata; this comment retains the exact counts. A reversible instrumentation-only revert proof follows; production hot-path revert proof is inapplicable because no production function changed."
  "2026-10-16T09:23:33.089Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural instrumentation revert proof: changed only instrumentCapacityModule to return source unchanged; node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern=\"opt-in tracing\" test/capacity.acceptance.ts failed 0/1 with TRACE_MISSING_broadcast. Restored the function after the test. This proves the new real-process attribution regression fails without its probes; it is not a hot-path performance-repair proof. Full linked acceptance before the revert passed 2/2; required npm/Bun gates will validate the restored function. Production functions and limits remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-16T09:36:36.098Z",codex-agent,"Required isolated-identity npm run release:check passes on its first attempt: 620/620 coverage tests, zero fail/cancel/skip/todo; 37 configured sources, statements/lines 90.91%, branches 81.10%, functions 94.17% at unchanged thresholds; capacity acceptance 2/2 including restored live tracing; packed current/minimum npm/native-Bun consumers 4/4; production audit zero vulnerabilities; changelog/date/publish-attestation and remaining gates pass. Canonical fleet metadata supplied through PM_FLEET_ROOT (readonly); its focused preflight passed 34/34. Starting isolated Bun gate serially."
  "2026-10-16T09:51:15.194Z",codex-agent,"Both required release gates pass on first attempts. Isolated npm: 620/620 coverage tests, 37 configured sources S/L 90.91%, B 81.10%, F 94.17%. Isolated Bun: 620/620, S/L 90.91%, B 81.15%, F 94.17%. Each has zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo, capacity acceptance 2/2, packed current/minimum npm/native-Bun consumers 4/4, production audit zero, remaining static/changelog/release metadata checks green, unchanged thresholds. Final docs: docs/capacity/2026-10-16-local.md and docs/capacity.md. Clarifications: B3 pre-command uptime load was 8.24/5.66/7.01; 9.18/5.90/7.08 is the harness after-build load. The 2071.0 ms lock-acquisition lower bound includes open/retry and payload-write scheduling, so shared-lock contention is an implementation-supported inference; failed attempts, I/O and scheduling are not separately counted. The observed pre-append SDK phase alone exceeds the SLO. The upstream draft remains unfiled. No production performance function, SDK pin or SLO changed. Tracker validation returned ok with metadata/trust/path warnings and zero history drift; no history was repaired or rewritten. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress. Next: push this evidence and await PR checks, with larger rungs unmeasured after the 100-subscriber breach."
  "2026-10-16T14:21:27.856Z",codex-agent,"Folding the three open review findings from PR #211 into its superseding PR #214. docs/capacity.md already links pm-cli#1485; correcting the local report and requiring a matching in-window index-lock record for every committed CLI write. Regression coverage will check complete multi-write populations, missing records, unrelated items, window bounds, HTTP writes and uncommitted writes; behavioural revert proof and both unchanged release gates follow. Historical draft comments describe the state at their timestamps; the current upstream issue is https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1485."
  "2026-10-16T14:21:54.764Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof for PR #214: reverted only stageSummary to HEAD while retaining the new tests, then ran node --test test/capacity-trace.test.ts. Result: 3 pass, 1 fail; the missing-CLI-lock regression fails with ERR_ASSERTION Missing expected exception. Restored stageSummary; the fixed suite passes 4/4. The error code is TRACE_MISSING_index-lock and the message identifies write sequence and item id. Complete traces retain multiple matching locks, including boundary records; unrelated or out-of-window locks cannot satisfy another committed write. HTTP writes need no index-lock probe; uncommitted writes are excluded."
  "2026-10-16T15:13:56.729Z",codex-agent,"PR #214 review follow-up validation passes on first attempts through the linked runner: npm run release:check (1483.426 s) and bun run release:check (1545.477 s), isolated HOME and global/system Git identity, readonly canonical fleet metadata. Each passes 648/648 coverage tests with zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo, 2/2 real-process capacity scenarios, 4/4 packed current/minimum npm/native-Bun consumers, zero production vulnerabilities and all static/changelog/release metadata checks. All 39 configured source files reported: npm S/L 92.47%, B 81.00%, F 96.02%; Bun S/L 92.47%, B 81.06%, F 96.02%. Thresholds remain 92.07/92.07/80.5/94.59. No local timing failures occurred. The behavioural revert base was f163153; only stageSummary was reverted, yielding 3 pass/1 fail, then restored for all successful runs. Linked focused execution passes 4/4. Initial inherited-test trust refusal was resolved by reviewing and acknowledging the existing commands in this clone; test-result tracking remains disabled by project policy, so this comment retains the results. docs/capacity.md already linked pm-cli#1485; docs/capacity/2026-10-16-local.md now links it instead of saying unfiled. Preparing the code and append-only tracker evidence for push, then waiting for exact-head GitHub checks; PR #211 can be superseded by #214. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-19T17:42:50.388Z",codex-agent,"2026-10-19: Reusing this investigation for companion pm-cli-website-ghe1. Measure the untraced 100 -> 1000 -> 3000 subscriber ladder against the current public package revision, one synthetic project per rung, five HTTP and five pinned-CLI writer lanes, five writes per lane, 2000 ms SLO. Capture host load/resources before each rung, use unique external report prefixes and stop at the first failed rung. Disposable test database and temporary project roots only. Documentation and tracker evidence only; no runtime fixes or hosted operations. Dependency installation required removing ambient npm allow-scripts configuration while retaining npm ci --ignore-scripts."
  "2026-10-19T17:44:27.361Z",codex-agent,"Measured revision 8e9cc9713778f9ff945eb28c57d827d20cf75995 with pinned pm CLI 2026.10.19. STOP at 100 subscribers: 50/50 committed writes; to-all p50/p95/p99/max 483.6/1643.4/2274.1/2274.1 ms, 0 lost and 100 duplicate receipts (one per subscriber), zero write failures/disconnects/server errors. Server peak RSS 187.1 MiB, CPU p95 22.4% of one core, event-loop p99 44.9 ms; generator CPU 3.2%, event-loop p99 28.4 ms; Postgres peak 20 server/21 total of 100 maximum. Pre-rung load 6.44/7.83/11.33, harness initial 8.54/8.23/11.43, final 10.91/8.83/11.51 on four CPUs. Harness names host scheduling or I/O pressure, cause unproven. Neither fd exhaustion nor generator CPU saturation was observed; fd limits unchanged at 1048576. No passing rung or quiet-host server ceiling established. 1000 and 3000 intentionally unmeasured. No runtime changes. Documentation and required gates follow."
