  "2026-10-19T19:51:39.877Z",codex-agent,"Accepted exact implementation head ad380c7 CI receipts: Node 22 npm and Bun each 677/677 tests, 2/2 capacity, 4/4 packed consumers, zero vulnerabilities; coverage S/L 92.40, branches 81.60, functions 95.28, all 40 sources. Node 26 npm: same counts, S/L 92.40, branches 81.60, functions 96.17; Bun: same counts, S/L 92.40, branches 81.64, functions 96.17. All zero fail/cancel/skip/todo, all thresholds unchanged. CI run 39310211835. These accepted CI receipts replace no failed local receipt: local npm attempt 2 has one known E2E cancellation; local Bun passes all 677 tests plus 2 capacity cases, coverage and audit, then its 1800000 ms linked-command budget terminates packed acceptance. No full local green is claimed."
  "2026-10-19T19:55:13.137Z",codex-agent,"CI provenance verified: PR head ad380c7cb294be24aedecf268cb2d0d110b06d5c and CI merge checkout 77727f61130a49919f54f9376a661abe41f51f55 have identical Git tree eafbb7a7e3cb2934c10369bd61086033b1018d28. All four full gate receipts therefore validate the exact implementation and tests; final pending edits are evidence and tracker metadata only. The three implementation claims are released and every item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-19T21:47:52.331Z",codex-agent,"PR #226 review round retained local capacity failure: full Bun release gate passed 682/682 coverage tests and all coverage floors, then the untraced 20-subscriber, five-writer capacity smoke reached its unchanged every-delivery <=2000 ms assertion and failed. Its preceding assertions prove five commits, zero failed writes, loss, duplicates or disconnected subscribers, and five complete latency samples. The traced capacity scenario passed, so acceptance was 1/2 and the full local Bun gate stopped before audit/packed acceptance. Earlier full npm gate passed all stages, including both capacity scenarios and all four packed consumers. Do not relabel this failure as green or infer a host-load root cause without attribution. Capturing an unchanged focused report; the existing mixed-writer latency follow-up remains open."
  "2026-10-19T21:49:18.424Z",codex-agent,"Unchanged focused reproduction after the local Bun SLO miss passed: 20 subscribers, five writer lanes, one write each, the same 2000 ms SLO/drain, five complete committed samples, maximum/p99 490.87744140625 ms, zero loss, duplicates or server errors. This is a separate observation, not a replacement for the failed full-gate receipt, and does not attribute its root cause. Rerunning the exact isolated Bun capacity stage without changing code; current-head full CI gates will provide independent npm/Bun acceptance."
  "2026-10-19T21:51:54.437Z",codex-agent,"The exact isolated bun run accept:capacity retry passed 2/2 with zero failure/cancellation/skip/todo at unchanged thresholds and code. Both the full-gate SLO miss and later focused successes remain distinct in the capacity report. Synthetic reproduction report SHA-256: 076129394bda41e88488f9116f3b4c46cc654300301d19d922c7af14993c22ea. Root cause remains unattributed; no latency certification is inferred. Remote full-gate receipts are maintained at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/226 for current-head verification."
  "2026-10-20T14:56:55.274Z",codex-agent,"Reusing this item for the thousand-subscriber fan-out work; companion pm-cli-website-ghe1 stays read-only. Baseline 5346b64 already serializes JSON once per project event, but writes strings per response, ignores backpressure, has no SSE wire cursor/replay, and does no per-event authorization reads. Plan: shared UTF-8 frames, bounded burst batching and client queues, project-scoped resumable replay, per-subscriber authorization preserved with shared membership reads. Compare interleaved A/B/A/B mixed HTTP and pinned-CLI writers at 100/1000/3000 using CPU microseconds, encoded bytes, loop delay and host load; no hosted access."
  "2026-10-20T15:05:33.382Z",codex-agent,"Shared-frame batching and bounded queues are implemented. Focused regressions prove one serialization and one shared Buffer for a 3000-viewer burst, ordered drain without retrying a false write, isolated slow-client eviction, and exact missed-frame resume. A real-Postgres HTTP adversarial test passes for stranger denial, cross-project cursor rejection, direct/group access and revocation; no private frame reaches denied viewers. Test-only CPU probes cover the same synchronous service boundaries before/after, excluding database await and scheduling. Interleaved mixed-writer measurements are running against the disposable test service."
  "2026-10-20T15:06:47.212Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only prepareFanout with the previous shared-string/direct-response loop (no other production function changed, no SDK mocks) makes the new response and real-HTTP regressions fail. The candidate function was restored byte-for-byte afterwards. Command: node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test test/sse-fanout.test.ts test/sse-fanout-access.test.ts. Baseline profiling confirms JSON already had O(1) serialization, zero per-subscriber tracker reads, zero per-event authorization queries, and no explicit response callbacks; repeated string encoding/socket bookkeeping and ignored backpressure remain the per-subscriber work. Candidate keeps per-project membership reads shared while applying authorization to each sink."
  "2026-10-20T15:16:06.529Z",codex-agent,"Review found that replay retention must not activate watchers for arbitrary peer-bus projects. Added an O(1) served-project guard, a no-allocation regression for unknown projects, and cleanup of expired project receipt maps. Serialization failures cannot advance a resume cursor. Exploratory measurements used the initial candidate; certification will use a fresh A/B/A/B sequence after these corrections. Added a real-production-process non-git tracker scenario for CLI commits while the last SSE viewer is forcibly disconnected. Revert proof currently fails 6 of 7 focused assertions under the old direct-write behavior, with the candidate restored."
  "2026-10-20T15:23:44.867Z",codex-agent,"The production-process last-viewer resume regression passes: 1/1, three independent CLI updates made with zero connected viewers are replayed exactly once; the already-received update is absent on resume. The tracker is explicitly non-git. Test-only measurements now separate synchronous service CPU from non-overlapping event-loop-turn CPU (to include deferred response work without per-response callbacks), and JSON bytes from framed UTF-8 bytes for measured mutations. Final comparisons wait for the complete final presence snapshot before resetting counters."
  "2026-10-20T15:29:13.537Z",codex-agent,"Final behavioral revert proofs: reverting only prepareFanout to the former shared-string/direct-write loop fails 10 of 11 focused tests (one unrelated stall-timer case still passes). Independently removing only the per-viewer authorization check in writeFanoutBatch fails the real-Postgres HTTP adversarial test with an observed revoked-viewer private-frame leak (true versus false), while preserving framing/replay. Both candidate functions were restored byte-for-byte. Large replay is chunked through the same shared queue: a catch-up near 2 MiB passes without disconnect or duplicate, despite exceeding the 1 MiB client queue budget. The final comparison rejects any runtime/probe artifact hash drift between runs."
  "2026-10-20T15:39:31.688Z",codex-agent,"The original comparison stopped on fixture cleanup at 1000, so its partial data is not certification. Focused fixture lifecycle: 1000-identity cleanup took about 3.7 seconds; 3000 took 10.7 seconds, with successful root removal. The original observer client imposed a five-second query timeout on those FK cascades. Cleanup now uses a separate bounded 60-second SQL budget and retains an exact synthetic ownership receipt on failure. Resource-probe timeouts, delivery SLO, loss/duplicate assertions and release thresholds are unchanged. A narrowly scoped read of this task interval found no remaining synthetic Capacity project rows. Restarted the complete immutable A/B/A/B ladder; it asserts total elapsed time remains below one hour."
  "2026-10-20T16:03:09.147Z",codex-agent,"Authorization review reproduced an in-flight snapshot race: later events could use a membership result read before revocation. A behavioral revert of only the batch boundaries fails both the late-event and late-registration regressions. Flushes now capture event sequence and viewer registration before the SQL read; later events/viewers require a fresh decision, and an older failed read affects only its captured audience. Focused response/HTTP/real-tracker suite passes 30/30. The non-git resume test keeps every five-second receipt assertion but gives its new fixture lifecycle a 120-second outer budget (its instrumented preflight took 59.9 seconds). The completed preflight is explicitly red: 696/700 pass, 3 fail and 1 cancelled, matching tracked catalog/startup pm-web-qdhx and graph pm-web-hqqp classes; no thresholds changed. Full npm and Bun release commands will run on the frozen runtime."
  "2026-10-20T16:09:26.161Z",codex-agent,"The SPA previously closed EventSource on every error, discarding its native Last-Event-ID. It now keeps the same source on transient errors; terminally closed streams use a fresh replacement and refresh existing live-view data paths, with project/source guards against stale callbacks. Tests execute the actual source callbacks in an isolated browser-like realm: 5/5 pass; removing only the transient-source guard is the browser behavioral revert. Server snapshot/registration boundary, late read failure, HTTP authorization and real-tracker focused checks pass 30/30. Preparing the frozen runtime and new A/B sequence with these required client and authorization corrections."
  "2026-10-20T16:11:21.574Z",codex-agent,"Browser behavioral revert completed: removing only the transient EventSource preservation guard fails 2/5 callback tests (the terminal/replacement cases still pass). Candidate restored; browser callbacks pass 5/5, and server/HTTP/real-tracker focused tests pass 30/30. The batch-boundary behavioral revert fails both the post-revocation-event and newly-granted-viewer cases. Frozen code includes event/registration snapshots, bounded shared replay chunks, scoped cleanup ownership receipts, and native browser cursor retention; remaining work is final A/B evidence and full release validation."
  "2026-10-20T17:03:56.742Z",codex-agent,"Freeze the comparison method with constant-count CPU scopes, actual event-frame counters and continuously refilled ten-slot startup below the default database pool size. A fifty-slot exploratory baseline ramp returned HTTP 500 before measurement, while the candidate completed 150000 mutation deliveries at 3000 viewers with zero lost, duplicate or disconnected deliveries. Startup and final full-presence deadlines remain unchanged; this measures an established subscriber population, not join-storm capacity. Safe setup phase codes and setup duration are retained. Lint caught two async cleanup flags; use abort state and idempotent stream cleanup without changing assertions."
  "2026-10-20T17:07:27.711Z",codex-agent,"The ten-slot exploratory baseline ramp also became invalid: an owned server health sample showed 2395 connections registered and 80 already disconnected before 3000 were established. Keep this as a setup failure with no CPU/latency sample. The comparison now aborts a ramp on an existing disconnected stream and records baseline setup failures while continuing A/B/A/B; every measured baseline and every candidate rung still strictly asserts all 50 commits, every delivery, zero loss, zero duplicates and zero disconnects. Never interpret unavailable baseline samples as zeros or a speedup."
  "2026-10-20T17:22:53.526Z",codex-agent,"The exploratory ten-slot interleaved sequence stopped on candidate SSE_STARTUP_TIMEOUT during 1000-viewer setup, before any measured writes for that rung. Do not publish it as a successful comparison. Restore the original harness cap of fifty simultaneous starts, continuously refilling accepted slots for both builds; the separate candidate 3000-viewer success used fifty. The ten-slot attempt allowed repeated large presence rounds during the longer ramp. No startup, presence, queue, delivery or correctness threshold changes. Freeze and repeat the complete sequence under the shared fifty-slot method."
  "2026-10-20T17:44:43.707Z",codex-agent,"The fifty-slot sequence also reached 1000 candidate streams but failed the 45-second final-presence readiness check before writers started. Preserve both failed methods. Add aggregate setup diagnostics (reader presence-count histogram, opened/disconnected counts, owned-server client count and process sample) with no identities or error messages. Add an explicit bounded comparison-only 120-second warm-up option; default connection readiness remains 15 seconds and final presence 45 seconds for release acceptance, with all production pool/queue bounds and delivery SLOs unchanged. Warm-up is excluded from measured fan-out CPU/latency and its elapsed time is reported. Run one diagnostic rung before freezing a new interleaved comparison."
  "2026-10-20T17:56:30.227Z",codex-agent,"The explicit warm-up diagnostic completed 50000 deliveries at 1000 viewers with zero lost/duplicate events; unoptimized setup took 279887 ms. Source inspection found generator work duplicated per reader: scanning full data for absent header fields and allocating the roster match array per socket. Parse headers separately and cache eight exact roster frames while keeping all network receipts independent. Twelve harness tests pass, including two real sockets with a withheld final byte; reverting only the cache function fails that test 1/1 and byte-for-byte restoration passes. Validate optimized 3000-viewer setup before freezing the final A/B sequence."
  "2026-10-20T18:12:47.494Z",codex-agent,"Final runtime refinement: a drained response with neither queued bytes nor an unsubmitted journal frame now performs no membership query. Sixty-four authorized sinks prove zero reads for empty connected drains, one read for a private batch, no extra reads after its completed writes, then a fresh read rejecting a revoked viewer before the next private frame. Focused runtime/browser/real-tracker/harness suite passes 33/33. Exact behavioral reversions fail 14/15 for event preparation, 1/1 for empty drains, and 1/1 for reader caching, followed by byte-for-byte restoration. Comparison-only setup uses ten slots and 120-second readiness; release defaults remain fifty slots and 15/45-second readiness, with all delivery thresholds unchanged. Cache up to 128 exact rosters within 64 MiB and publish hit/miss counts. Include aligned whole-server CPU totals to expose asynchronous costs outside scoped timers."
  "2026-10-20T18:24:31.740Z",codex-agent,"Freeze comparison setup at sixteen simultaneous starts, leaving three ordinary query slots after the default pool listener; both variants use the same 120-second warm-up and bounded reader cache. Ordinary release defaults and every latency/coverage/duplication floor remain unchanged. The ten-slot diagnostic remains separate exploratory evidence. Source/server/frontend typechecks, 33 focused tests, zero duplication and docstrings pass. Run the existing CI workflow on the frozen commit for full npm and Bun release gates under Node 22 and 26, keeping their extra CPU processes off the comparison host. Primary A/B runs retain immutable artifact hashes and a one-hour bound."
  "2026-10-20T19:50:42.703Z",codex-agent,"Fresh-permission regression: a heartbeat could flush queued private data while the next authorization read was pending. Heartbeats now preserve the queue until that decision; the targeted function-only revert fails 1/1. Hardened the load generator against buffered connected frames arriving after an expired startup deadline (revert fails 1/1). Client readers now use bounded worker threads, independent real sockets and receipt timestamps; the two-worker withholding test fails 1/1 when the measurement phase is reverted. Reverting only prepareFanout to the old direct shared-string loop fails 15/16 core/access cases. All restored sources pass 36/36 focused tests, with zero failed, skipped or canceled tests. The preceding runtime passed both complete npm and Bun release gates in both Node 22 and 26 CI jobs; the corrected runtime will receive fresh full gates."
  "2026-10-20T20:27:50.590Z",codex-agent,"The frozen worker-reader sequence completed all eight 100/1000-viewer runs and the first 3000-viewer baseline with exact delivery, then stopped before candidate measurement at 3000: project verification returned HTTP 500 around 1800 connected sockets, with zero observed disconnects. This is a setup failure, not a passing capacity sample. Preserve it as exploratory evidence. Diagnose initial verification separately with eight startup slots for more default-pool headroom, retaining the same 120-second warm-up and every delivery/auth/queue threshold. Runtime 90ac471 passed all four full npm/Bun release gates under Node 22/26: 712 suite tests, two capacity acceptance tests and four packed scenarios per gate, unchanged floors."
  "2026-10-20T20:41:11.829Z",codex-agent,"Establishing 3000 viewers with ordinary incremental rosters remained unstable: the eight-slot diagnostic disconnected readers during setup. Added an opt-in test-preload setup control for both builds: defer incremental presence until all real authenticated sockets connect, release one actual full roster through production fan-out, and require every socket receipt before resetting counters. Ordinary release joining remains unchanged. Real two-socket hold/release/normal-presence test passes; reverting only instrumentCapacitySetup fails 1/1, then byte-for-byte restoration passes. The controlled 3000 pilot delivered all 150000 mutation frames with 50 committed writes, zero loss/duplicates/disconnects; four HTTP acknowledgments failed under the 20-second experiment deadline. Comparison-only acknowledgment budget is now 120 seconds, separately from the unchanged 1-second latency verdict and ordinary 20-second release writer budget. Raw writer receipts retain safe error names/codes. This measures established fan-out; ordinary join-storm failures remain a published production limitation."
